{"approval":{"approval_subject_sha256":"sha256:5df935696336030349b2959325e9e256b45f926aa5fdb983c31c931c23fba119","approval_url":"https://github.com/sagikazarmark/excalidraw-render.orig/issues/152#issuecomment-5614876369","approved_at":"2026-09-10","approved_by":"sagikazarmark"},"assets":[],"case_id":"focused.font-families-virgil-lilita-comic.v1","comparison":{"comparator_profiles":[],"viewer_profiles":[{"digest":"sha256:3bb429c3a816f7415e1ed8691d2b63b1993e10f71d16483a8737909eae59b13d","id":"reference-evidence.browser-raster.v1","scope":"reference evidence repeatability only"}]},"compatibility_revision":1,"coverage":[{"identity":"font.virgil","role":"primary"},{"identity":"font.lilita-one","role":"primary"},{"identity":"font.comic-shanns","role":"primary"},{"identity":"font.reserved-name-alias","role":"primary"},{"identity":"text.align","role":"primary"},{"identity":"reference.direct-png","role":"primary"},{"identity":"reference.svg","role":"primary"}],"crops":[],"determinism":{"animation_offset_microseconds":0,"fresh_process_runs":2},"exceptions":[{"approving_issue":"https://github.com/sagikazarmark/excalidraw-render.orig/issues/152","format":"png","max_changed_pixels":2060,"minimum_ssim_bits":"3fef4977608aa6c3","reason":"Sub-pixel glyph coverage. The 19 elements in Virgil, Lilita One, Comic Shanns and Excalifont are positioned by each family's metadata metrics and shaped with the bundled faces (evidenced on #152): the SVG document matches the official export under one rasterizer (0 changed pixels, SSIM 1.0), the scene extent and all 38 baselines agree to the last digit, and in the direct PNG every glyph's horizontal placement agrees; only glyph ink differs between the renderer's rasterizer and the browser's canvas. The canvas snaps each line's baseline to the nearest whole pixel while the renderer fills the outlines at the exact fractional baseline the SVG declares (#169): the vertical ink centroid of every line is displaced by round(baseline) - baseline, 0.38 px for Excalifont and Virgil at 20 px, 0.28 for Virgil at 36 px, 0.47 and -0.35 for Lilita One at 20 and 36 px, 0.5 for Comic Shanns, so a text row's edge moves by at most one pixel and no glyph moves horizontally. The same class is recorded on #104, #105, #108, #110 and #153 for the other text-bearing cases.","region":"whole","variant":"default","viewer_profile":null}],"feature_tags":["element:text","font:virgil","font:lilita-one","font:comic-shanns","font:excalifont","text:align","text:line-height","format:svg","format:png"],"layer":"focused","license":{"copyright":"Copyright 2026 excalidraw-render contributors","expression":"MIT OR Apache-2.0"},"originating_issue":"https://github.com/sagikazarmark/excalidraw-render.orig/issues/152","provenance":{"byte_length":5542,"path":"evidence/provenance.json","sha256":"4ab8b06a6a59ef98b144afe3b2c6ed08168b026346c239cf94a202547a861f51"},"purpose":"Shape and position ordinary scene text in the three bundled families the corpus never evidenced, Virgil (fontFamily 1), Lilita One (7) and Comic Shanns (8), beside an Excalifont control: each family carries a two-line wrapped element at fontSize 20 and at 36 under every textAlign value, with the family's metadata line height (1.25, 1.15, 1.25), so the family metadata metrics that place each baseline, the stored width that anchors the centred and right-aligned lines, and the Reserved Font Name aliases the direct SVG embeds the Virgil and Lilita One subsets under (ExcalidrawRender-1, ExcalidrawRender-7) are observed against official evidence.","reference":{"asset_manifest":{"digest":"sha256:02685099e6a12632d77a3cac4c6d3acef291520e4fef93a675ee8be471245d9a","path":"tests/oracle/reference-profiles/revision-1-assets.json"},"profile":{"digest":"sha256:1e08a342359ac1c7eed1384b8e027a8289257b46bdccbbad3a9980e786136b71","path":"tests/oracle/reference-profiles/revision-1.json"},"scene_surface":{"digest":"sha256:22021bc4676f6c0d541921b22e8646f556e25e80d8f339cda457abd7d2c8deac","path":"tests/oracle/sc